# track/docs-reskin scope manifest
#
# MULTI-TRACK PROTOCOL rule 2: a track is a branch plus this file. Every path a
# commit on track/docs-reskin touches must match one of the globs below, and
# scripts/qa/locked_paths_gate.mjs fails CI otherwise.
#
# Glob forms: an exact path; a trailing slash for a whole directory; ** for any
# depth and * for one segment.
#
# Declared by the owner in FS_MULTITRACK_PROTOCOL_V2_Prompt.md, JOB 4(a).

docs/RESKIN_BOUNDARY.md
docs/records/reviews/FIX_LIST_2026-07-26.md
SUBMISSION_DOSSIER.md
GAME_FACTS.md
COMPLIANCE_WATCH.md
WRS_MASTER_DOCUMENT.md

# The brief declared `docs/records/tracks/`, the whole directory. Narrowed to
# THIS track's own manifest, because the whole directory is also in
# track/quality-sweep's manifest and rule 3 requires parallel tracks to be
# provably disjoint. Neither track needs the directory: both manifests and both
# briefs are committed on main by the integrator before either track starts.
docs/records/tracks/docs-reskin.manifest

# Rule 8 requires a track session report, and convention (a) requires one of
# every session, but `reports/` is in neither manifest as the brief wrote them,
# so a track literally could not write its report. Resolved with a per-track
# report directory rather than by sharing reports/SESSION_REPORT.md: disjoint by
# construction, and it is what makes rule 8's "resolve report conflicts by
# concatenation" mechanical instead of a merge argument. The integrator
# concatenates these into reports/SESSION_REPORT.md on main.
reports/tracks/docs-reskin/
